framewatch.language.uk_UA=Українська
framewatch.language.tip=Cycle Auto / English / Ukrainian for FrameWatch only. Auto follows Ukrainian Minecraft languages, otherwise English. Minecraft's language and resources are not changed.
framewatch.unit.ms=ms
framewatch.unit.s=s
framewatch.unit.px=px
framewatch.unit.fps=FPS
framewatch.unit.MiB=MiB
framewatch.unit.MiBps=MiB/s
framewatch.scale=HUD scale
framewatch.scale.tip=Scale both panels from 0.50 to 2.50 in steps of 0.05. Small windows may fit the HUD at a smaller scale.
framewatch.opacity=Panel opacity
framewatch.opacity.tip=Background opacity: 0 is transparent, 1 is opaque. Text stays readable.
framewatch.enabled=HUD enabled
framewatch.enabled.tip=Hide or show the HUD. Frame collection continues while hidden.
framewatch.hideWithF1=Hide with F1
framewatch.hideWithF1.tip=Respect Minecraft's Hide GUI setting.
framewatch.textShadow=Text shadow
framewatch.textShadow.tip=Enable a shadow behind HUD text.
framewatch.leftAnchor=Main anchor
framewatch.leftAnchor.tip=Cycle the main panel's screen corner. Position offsets are measured from that corner.
framewatch.rightAnchor=Profiler anchor
framewatch.rightAnchor.tip=Cycle the profiler panel's screen corner independently.
framewatch.anchor.TOP_LEFT=Top left
framewatch.anchor.TOP_RIGHT=Top right
framewatch.anchor.BOTTOM_LEFT=Bottom left
framewatch.anchor.BOTTOM_RIGHT=Bottom right
framewatch.textRefresh=Text refresh
framewatch.textRefresh.tip=Refresh HUD text every 125–1000 ms. This does not change frame collection.
framewatch.showTitles=Titles
framewatch.showTitles.tip=Show panel headings. Disable for a compact FPS and frametime display.
framewatch.showFps=FPS
framewatch.showFps.tip=Show measured FPS as a standalone row when the FPS graph is off. With the graph on, FPS appears above it.
framewatch.showFrameTime=Frametime
framewatch.showFrameTime.tip=Show frame duration as a standalone row when its graph is off. With the graph on, the current duration appears above it.
framewatch.showStatistics=Statistics
framewatch.showStatistics.tip=Show rolling frame percentiles and low-FPS statistics.
framewatch.showMemory=RAM (JVM heap)
framewatch.showMemory.tip=Show used/max JVM heap as a standalone row when its graph is off. With the graph on, RAM appears above it. Not native memory or VRAM.
framewatch.showDirectMemory=Direct buffers (not VRAM)
framewatch.showDirectMemory.tip=Show the JVM's tracked off-heap direct buffers in native RAM. These buffers are only a subset of native memory, not total process RAM, not JVM heap and not GPU video memory (VRAM).
framewatch.showDirectMemory.tooltip=Show the JVM's tracked off-heap direct buffers in native RAM. These buffers are only a subset of native memory, not total process RAM, not JVM heap and not GPU video memory (VRAM).
framewatch.showAllocation=Allocation
framewatch.showAllocation.tip=Show measured allocation rate when supported by the JVM.
framewatch.showGc=Garbage collection
framewatch.showGc.tip=Show measured JVM garbage collection activity.
framewatch.showHardware=Hardware
framewatch.showHardware.tip=Show available hardware information. Unsupported values remain unavailable; no readings are invented.
framewatch.showEnvironment=Environment
framewatch.showEnvironment.tip=Show runtime and rendering environment information.
framewatch.showProfiler=Right CPU phase panel
framewatch.showProfiler.tip=Show the separate right-hand panel of measured CPU phase timings. Its anchor and position remain independently adjustable.
framewatch.hud.scale=Scale:
framewatch.showFpsGraph=FPS graph
framewatch.showFpsGraph.tip=Group current FPS above its graph; hide the duplicate summary row. The curve shows bucket averages; Scale labels the vertical maximum.
framewatch.showMemoryGraph=RAM graph (JVM heap)
framewatch.showMemoryGraph.tip=Group used/max JVM heap above its graph; hide the duplicate summary row. Samples once per second. Not process RAM or VRAM.
framewatch.showGraph=Frametime graph
framewatch.showGraph.tip=Group current frame duration above its graph without a duplicate summary row. Scale below is the vertical maximum, not the current value.
framewatch.showGraphEvents=Graph events
framewatch.showGraphEvents.tip=Show graph event information when the graph is enabled.
framewatch.graphWidth=Graph width
framewatch.graphWidth.tip=Logical graph width from 100 to 400 pixels, before HUD scaling.
framewatch.graphHeight=Graph height
framewatch.graphHeight.tip=Logical graph height from 30 to 140 pixels, before HUD scaling.
framewatch.graphWindow=Graph duration
framewatch.graphWindow.tip=Time span displayed by the graph: 1–30 seconds. Independent of the statistics window.
framewatch.graphMax=Graph axis
framewatch.graphMax.tip=Drag all the way left for Auto; otherwise set the upper axis limit to 30–250 ms.
framewatch.graphRefresh=Graph refresh
framewatch.graphRefresh.tip=Refresh the graph every 16–200 ms. Collection still records every presented frame.
framewatch.window=Statistics window
framewatch.window.tip=Rolling statistics duration: 1–30 seconds in this editor. Retained history is not cleared.
framewatch.target=Target FPS
framewatch.target.tip=0 selects Auto, using the FPS cap/display refresh. A positive value sets the frame budget; this does not limit Minecraft FPS.
framewatch.warmup=Warmup
framewatch.warmup.tip=Exclude 0–5000 ms after a world change or focus regain from normal measurements.
framewatch.longFrame=Long-frame threshold
framewatch.longFrame.tip=Mark frames exceeding this 10–100 ms threshold AND twice the target frame budget.
framewatch.preset.minimal=FPS + frametime
framewatch.preset.minimal.tip=Only FPS and frametime: no titles, graph, profiler or other blocks. Measurement settings are preserved.
framewatch.preset.graph=FPS + graph
framewatch.preset.graph.tip=Only FPS, frametime and the graph. No separate profiler panel or extra blocks.
framewatch.preset.full=Full
framewatch.preset.full.tip=Enable all measured blocks and graph events, but not unavailable hardware information. Measurement settings are preserved.
framewatch.position=Move panels
framewatch.position.tip=Drag the real HUD panels. Enable the HUD and desired blocks first. No sample telemetry is used.
framewatch.reset=Reset HUD
framewatch.reset.tip=Reset only HUD appearance, blocks and positions. Measurement options and retained history are unchanged.
framewatch.page.tip=Previous/next page. You can also use the mouse wheel or Page Up/Page Down.
framewatch.done.tip=Save settings and return. Escape also saves; there is no cancel/revert action.
framewatch.position.help=Drag either panel to move it. Done or Escape saves and returns.
framewatch.position.hidden=No visible panels. Return to settings and enable the HUD and desired blocks.
framewatch.saveFailed=[FrameWatch] Could not save settings. Your edits remain active for this session. Check the log, configuration folder permissions and free disk space.

